WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.710
So, now that we have the skeleton of the

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:03.470
website built out, how do you now

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.390
improve the look and feel of it? Well,

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:06.630
that's all built through this concept

00:00:06.640 --> 00:00:08.470
called a design system. To give you an

00:00:08.480 --> 00:00:10.630
example, if you come from this skeleton

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:12.230
that you made, which is this pretty

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:14.550
generic AI vibe coded website with this

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.230
blue gradients and this font, what we

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:18.070
use internally is this design system

00:00:18.080 --> 00:00:20.150
called /robo, which I'll also provide

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.630
below if you just want to test it out

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.110
and adopt it for your own brand. You can

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:24.390
see that with just one prompt, we

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.590
basically transformed that website into

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.510
this one with its custom fonts. I have

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.710
the Dodo font in here. I have the dot

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.030
matrix visual on the side, and we'll

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:34.110
improve this some more, but I just

00:00:34.120 --> 00:00:35.750
wanted to illustrate that basically what

00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:38.270
I asked Claude to do is to use the Robo

00:00:38.280 --> 00:00:40.790
design system and change it so that it

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:42.750
properly redesigns it to this version,

00:00:42.760 --> 00:00:44.910
which is now more custom and is no

00:00:44.920 --> 00:00:47.310
longer generic AI. But obviously, what I

00:00:47.320 --> 00:00:49.430
want to teach you is not just give you

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.710
this pre-built Robo design system

00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:53.630
because I want you to understand how to

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.390
create your own. And for you to create

00:00:55.400 --> 00:00:57.630
your own design system, you also have to

00:00:57.640 --> 00:00:59.710
develop your own sense of taste. And in

00:00:59.720 --> 00:01:01.110
this world of AI where you can just

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.630
pretty much generate anything, having a

00:01:02.640 --> 00:01:03.990
clear sense of taste is actually going

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:06.230
to give you a lot of advantage as we

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:07.950
move forward. And to me, developing your

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.870
sense of taste is simply coming from

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.430
seeing a lot of examples so that you can

00:01:12.440 --> 00:01:14.430
pick and choose what really inspires you

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:15.910
and to pick out the elements that you

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:18.150
would want for your own design. So, what

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:20.310
I provided below is this design systems

00:01:20.320 --> 00:01:22.310
toolkit, which you can just copy in your

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:25.030
workspace, and this contains 35 complete

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:27.150
fundamentally different websites so that

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:28.950
you can just pick and choose which ones

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:31.310
you would want to use and iterate on

00:01:31.320 --> 00:01:33.070
them or change them so that you already

00:01:33.080 --> 00:01:34.790
have the building blocks in order to

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:36.350
create what it is that you need. To give

00:01:36.360 --> 00:01:38.150
a few examples, this one's a website

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:39.790
with a bit of a security posture, and

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.390
you can see we have some nice animation

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.630
in the background there, and you can

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:44.070
adopt that as well. This one's a

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:46.550
template for a voice AI agency, which if

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:48.430
we scroll down here, that also includes

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:50.470
some nicely animated cards. This one's

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:51.950
appropriate if you're a bit more into

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.790
design and you want that minimalistic

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.390
style. You have this design system which

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.270
is pretty good for e-commerce stores,

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.070
and there's a lot of options here that

00:01:59.080 --> 00:02:00.750
would really just grab your attention if

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:02.870
you want to have like a bit of a change

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.670
in terms of the design. So, feel free to

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:06.469
browse around. This one is one of my

00:02:06.479 --> 00:02:08.190
personal favorites. It has that nice

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:09.950
effect which you can just adopt for any

00:02:09.960 --> 00:02:11.870
of your builds. And there's 35 more of

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:13.310
those for you to just get some

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:15.070
inspiration. Now, for you to customize

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:16.870
those templates and those design systems

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:19.110
further, I also included this palettes,

00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:20.670
this color palettes toolkit, so that you

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:21.949
can get inspired and also get some

00:02:21.959 --> 00:02:24.070
references on some well-known brands for

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.030
their color palettes as well as their

00:02:26.040 --> 00:02:27.750
own design systems. So, for example, for

00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:29.270
Apple here, if I open it, this gives you

00:02:29.280 --> 00:02:31.550
a lot of building blocks to make a more

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.590
of an Apple aesthetic. You also have

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:35.470
Airbnb in here. You have Uber, you have

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:36.990
Starbucks, you have PlayStation, and

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:38.630
dozens of other brands which you can

00:02:38.640 --> 00:02:40.630
just adopt and use. So, using these

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:42.310
artifacts, how do we now create our own

00:02:42.320 --> 00:02:44.310
design system? Well, it's really really

00:02:44.320 --> 00:02:46.230
simple. So, if I go down and actually

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:48.230
find the one that I want, let's say this

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:49.830
data poem one. Once you have this whole

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.150
thing cloned to your workspace, which

00:02:51.160 --> 00:02:52.630
you can just grab it below, you can now

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.510
open this page where if you click on

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:56.190
copy reference and let's say we want to

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.870
combine that aesthetic with Airbnb's

00:02:58.880 --> 00:03:00.229
color palette, then we can just copy

00:03:00.239 --> 00:03:01.710
this as well. And what we're going to do

00:03:01.720 --> 00:03:03.470
is just make a skill called design

00:03:03.480 --> 00:03:05.630
system X, and you can just rename this

00:03:05.640 --> 00:03:07.070
to whatever it is that you want. And

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.750
we're just going to copy in here the

00:03:08.760 --> 00:03:10.830
color palette reference as well as the

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:12.509
design system reference. And essentially

00:03:12.519 --> 00:03:14.310
what we're doing here is we are

00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:16.390
systematizing this design system so that

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.070
the next time that we want to upgrade

00:03:18.080 --> 00:03:19.990
any build or any website that we want to

00:03:20.000 --> 00:03:21.509
that design system, then we can just

00:03:21.519 --> 00:03:23.270
invoke this skill and that will

00:03:23.280 --> 00:03:25.110
instantly turn that website that we

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:27.150
built or any piece of software into the

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:28.990
aesthetics of that design system that we

00:03:29.000 --> 00:03:30.550
built. The reason why this is also so

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:32.390
powerful is that later on when we want

00:03:32.400 --> 00:03:33.949
to add into this design system, which

00:03:33.959 --> 00:03:35.870
I'll show you more in a future module,

00:03:35.880 --> 00:03:37.229
then what you now have is this skill

00:03:37.239 --> 00:03:39.310
which is effectively now going to be a

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:41.190
hub for all of the components and all of

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:42.910
the assets that you would like to store

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:44.630
and in the future make use of from

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.110
within this design system. To give an

00:03:46.120 --> 00:03:48.030
example for the Robo design system, you

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.790
may notice these agency price that I use

00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:52.030
a lot in a lot of our materials, and

00:03:52.040 --> 00:03:54.150
those are actually part of this /robo

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:55.510
skill. So that whenever I need to use

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:57.550
them, then Claude code knows exactly

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.030
where to find these components. There

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.590
are also other components that are a bit

00:04:00.600 --> 00:04:01.790
more advanced, and I'll go through how

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:03.350
to make these in just a bit. But you can

00:04:03.360 --> 00:04:05.270
see here that these sort of animations

00:04:05.280 --> 00:04:06.790
that you can just include in your builds

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:08.310
or any software product that you are

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:09.670
building just to make it a bit more

00:04:09.680 --> 00:04:11.550
engaging. These are all part of that

00:04:11.560 --> 00:04:13.510
/robo skill, which at this point are

00:04:13.520 --> 00:04:15.630
just reusable components that I can plug

00:04:15.640 --> 00:04:18.030
into any build depending on my needs.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:20.550
And so, now what you have is not just a

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.510
static design system, but an evolving

00:04:22.520 --> 00:04:23.909
one, right? You'll be able to create

00:04:23.919 --> 00:04:25.510
these animations, these modular

00:04:25.520 --> 00:04:27.470
components as you slowly build up and

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:30.030
tune the design system for your business

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.750
or your client. So now, back to this

00:04:31.760 --> 00:04:33.590
design system X that we just built a

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.310
skill around, you can see once it's done

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:37.550
that it now created that system X

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:39.350
template for us, and this is just a

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:41.230
sample of a website that it did. And

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:42.750
apart from creating a skill for the

